                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "For those who are looking for a no nonsense simulator for train operation this is one of the best games out there that I have played so far. The price is reasonable for what it is and the details that the simulator models is very good. As a part of the tutorial, the game links actual old British Rail training videos to learn about train operations, signalling, etc. I am American and I knew basically nothing about UK railroading whatsoever before using this simulator. Now after seeing the primary sources linked by the game as well as doing some of the routes my knowledge of UK railroading has greatly increased. I also now have the song \"Brainblast\" from the BR signalling video stuck in my head (iykyk).\r\n\r\nIf you are a fan of stopping passenger services, this game is for you. I was ignorant to the fact that UK trains used vacuum brakes well into the 20th century and to my knowledge this is the only sim that simulates vacuum braking systems properly. Handling the trains and making stops is challenging to master. I still cannot do it without the handicap of the brake status monitor on the HUD.",
